  "body": "## What changed\n\n- **Program gate, every post.** The machine check (`machine::check_ops`, which every post path runs through `verification_report`) now refuses a path carrying tap cycles on a machine whose `.mch` states `spindle.rigid_tapping: false`. The message names the op, the cycle count and the machine: `Tap1: 1 tap cycle(s) need rigid tapping, which Tormach 770M cannot do - use a tapping head or thread milling`. Before this, only `tormach.cps` read `machine.rigidTapping`, so a 770M posted through Fanuc or Haas wrote a G84 with no warning. The cycle is never converted to another cycle. `tormach.cps` is unchanged and keeps its own refusal for the standalone script path. The gate is `judge::tap_gate` (`crates/app/src/machine/judge.rs`).\n- **Schema validated.** A `rigid_tapping` value that isn't `true`, `false` or `null` now refuses the file by name, at the reader (`parse_mch`: `spindle.rigid_tapping must be true or false, not \"no\"`) and in the Machines pane's validator (key `spindle.rigid_tapping`). Before, `\"no\"` read as unstated, which means \"not limited\".\n- **Machines pane.** The Spindle group's \"Rigid tapping\" row now reads `yes`, `no - tap cycles are refused`, or `not stated - not limited`, instead of the raw `true`/`false`. The structural UI test was updated; no snapshot PNG changed.\n- **Machine files.** No `.mch` changed. Every Tormach mill and router already stated the value (#170, #618, #620): `true` on the four MX mills, `false` on the R8 M/M+ mills, the PCNC series and the routers. A new test pins the whole set. The lathes are unstated, so behaviour there is unchanged, and #795 tracks them.\n- **Docs.** `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` and `docs/MACHINE-ONBOARDING.md` describe the key. The decision is in `docs/decisions/786-rigid-tapping.md`: explicit on the Tormach files, absent means \"not limited\". Default-false was considered and dropped because it would change every non-Tormach machine.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests (new `crates/app/tests/rigid_tapping.rs`):\n- `a_tap_on_a_machine_that_cannot_rigid_tap_is_refused_by_name_whatever_the_post`: a tap job on the 770M through Tormach PathPilot, Fanuc and Haas, run through `posting::post_setup`. It is refused by name, no file is written, and the machine check names it. Fails with the gate line commented out (checked).\n- `a_tap_posts_where_rigid_tapping_is_stated_or_unstated`: the 1100MX on PathPilot and the generic VMC on Fanuc still post G84, and the check stays silent.\n- `rigid_tapping_must_be_a_boolean_or_the_file_is_refused_by_name`: both doors.\n- `the_machines_sheet_states_rigid_tapping_in_words`\n- `every_tormach_mill_and_router_file_states_rigid_tapping`\n- UI: `egui_app::tests::machines_pane::the_sheet_states_rigid_tapping_in_words` (AccessKit labels).\n\nSuites run on the final head (merged with v0.17.0), all green:\n- camcraft-app: rigid_tapping 5, machine 33, machine_library 11, machine_edit 12, posting 17, conformance 6, golden_cl 24, tormach_machines 6, tormach_post 10, tormach_routers 5, plasma_machine 6, carvera_machines 1. Earlier head, also green: fanuc_post 11, solid_law_goldens 1, heidenhain_block_form 4.\n- camcraft-post: all suites.\n- camcraft-ui lib `machines_pane` + `structural`: 11.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nThe 770MX G84 golden and every other golden are byte-identical; no golden file is in the diff.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full quick gate (the coordinator runs it) and the batch and release tiers.\n- A hand check of the Machines pane: the Rigid tapping row wording on a real window.\n- The Tormach lathes, which are left unstated (#795).\n- MCP: no new command. The refusal goes through the existing post tools via the same gate.\n\nChangelog: A tap cycle on a machine whose file says it cannot rigid-tap (the R8 Tormach mills, PCNC series, routers) is now refused by name at the post gate through every post, not only the Tormach one; `spindle.rigid_tapping` must be true or false, and the Machines pane states it in words (#786)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nfork synced at v0.17.0\n\nFixes #786\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
